meta:
  origin:
    # Data product / Snapshot
    title: World Population Historical Database (1991 borders)
    description: |-
      Annual population estimates for all polities from 1800 to 1938, re-expressed on 1991 political borders. The Federico–Tena World Population Historical Database re-estimates historical population series from first-hand sources and country-specific literature, and the 1991-borders layer re-allocates those series onto constant modern territories so that they join the United Nations series from 1950 onwards.

      Two methods build the 1991-borders layer. Where a modern country was created by the break-up of a larger polity, such as the post-Soviet republics, the parent's population is split between successors using their shares of the parent's population in 1950. Where a territory moved between two existing countries, such as Alsace-Lorraine, the transferred territory's population is estimated as a census-derived share of the origin country and then subtracted from it and added to the destination. Both methods leave continent and world totals unchanged.

      The November 2026 revision reworks the 1991-borders series. Germany, Poland and the Soviet successor states are rebuilt from period-specific province lists; Estonia, Latvia and Lithuania are now estimated directly from Russian statistical yearbooks instead of being given a share of the Soviet total; Ireland and the United Kingdom are split using a fixed 29% share for Northern Ireland; the Balkan territories the Ottoman Empire lost between 1878 and 1912 are re-apportioned among Greece, Bulgaria, Serbia, Montenegro and Albania; Aden and Bahrain are revised; and Saint Barthélemy is separated from Guadeloupe. The file also carries a reconciliation sheet documenting the shares used and checking that the rebuilt series still sum to the world total.

      Values are reported in thousands of people.
    date_published: "2026-11-04"
    version_producer: "November 2026 revision (1991 borders)"

    # Citation
    producer: Federico and Tena-Junguito
    citation_full: |-
